<title>SINGAPORE: Rotary 1st half net profit leaps.</title>
<headline>Rotary 1st half net profit leaps.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>						1996	  1995</p>
<p>    Net profit			    2.62   vs   0.50</p>
<p>    Profit per share (cents)	  1.30   vs   0.30</p>
<p>    Turnover			     54.90   vs  30.96</p>
<p>    Interest (income)		   0.49   vs   0.61</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		  0.07   vs   0.03</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  1.12   vs   1.02</p>
<p>    Income from associates	    1.16   vs   0.46</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			4.56   vs   1.09</p>
<p>    Tax				     1.28   vs   0.42</p>
<p>    Minority Interest		   0.67   vs   0.17</p>
<p>Note - Engineering and construction firm Rotary Engineering Ltd said it had received contracts amounting to S$42.3 million for the first six months. The group's overall performance was expected to remain profitable for the second half.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
